  "text": "Holy mother of god ....  \n\nThe Immaculate Conception vs. The Virgin Birth\n\nPeople frequently confuse these two distinct concepts:\n\n• The Immaculate Conception refers to Mary's conception in the womb of her mother, Saint Anne. It is about Mary being born without original sin.\n\n• The Virgin Birth refers to Jesus's conception in the womb of Mary through the power of the Holy Spirit, without a human father.\n\nSo describing the shift from seeking an external sign to becoming a willing vessel—mirroring Mary’s own response\n\n \"Let it be done to me according to your word\"\n\n\"Heavenly Father, the ultimate miracle is a heart entirely untainted by doubt and fully open to your presence. I step out of the way. Cleanse my heart of fear, make my spirit immaculate, and let me be a pure vessel for your love, your grace, and your work in this world. God, I’m not asking you to change my circumstances; I’m asking you to fill them. I open my hands and my heart to you. Do your work through me. Let your grace be born in my actions today.\"",
